        "text": "All required Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory.\n\nHere are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_invoice_fields.py** - Extracts vendor, date, total, and line-item fields from an invoice using AWS Textract.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_receipt_fields.py** - Extracts merchant, tax, total, and items from a receipt using AWS Textract.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] normalize_expense.py** - Normalizes extracted expense fields into a standard JSON schema.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] validate_document_fields.py** - Validates required structured fields and confidence scores.\n5. **[HELPER] document_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Structured Document Extraction using AWS.\n6. **[HELPER] document_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Structured Document Extraction.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] invoice_summary.py** - Summarizes extracted invoice fields.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] vendor_text_safety.py** - Moderates vendor notes or memo fields.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] invoice_note_translate.py** - Translates extracted invoice notes or descriptions using AWS Translate.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] expense_record_store.py** - Persists normalized expense records in a managed document store using AWS DynamoDB.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses a concrete external provider (AWS) and makes that provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files provide configuration, payload normalization, and response parsing utilities.",
